extend type Query {
    """
    Every stream that plays or prepares on this server instance now, one per playback session, in no fixed
    order. Ended and failed playback sessions are not listed; the server keeps no history of them. Requires a
    ServerAdmin. Every other caller gets FORBIDDEN, and so does a ServerAdmin's device-bound session.
    """
    activeStreams: [ActiveStream!]!
}

extend type Subscription {
    """
    An active stream started, changed its format attempt, playing state, position or produced range, or ended.
    Delivers the stream as the server reads it after the change, with activeStream null once it ended or failed.
    Requires a ServerAdmin. Every other caller gets FORBIDDEN, and so does a ServerAdmin's device-bound session.

    To build current state, subscribe first, then query activeStreams, and apply each change by
    playbackSessionId. One stream's changes arrive in the order they happened. A client may miss an
    intermediate state, but the last change it receives for a stream carries that stream's latest state.

    A change in a stream's producedRange alone fires a change for that stream at most once every 5 seconds, and
    only when the range differs by at least one media segment from the range that the stream's last change
    carried. Every other change carries the stream's current producedRange.
    """
    activeStreamsChanged: ActiveStreamChange
}

"One change to the active streams."
type ActiveStreamChange {
    playbackSessionId: ID!
    "The stream after the change, or null once it ended or failed."
    activeStream: ActiveStream
}

"One playback session that plays or prepares a stream now."
type ActiveStream {
    playbackSessionId: ID!
    "The viewer's Profile."
    profile: ActiveStreamProfile!
    "The device name that the viewer's sign-in gave, such as the app and device. Null when it gave none."
    deviceName: String
    mediaFileId: ID!
    """
    The movie or episode that the stream plays. Null for a media file without a matched movie or episode.
    Its selectedProfileState, and that of its season and series, describes the caller's selected Profile, not
    the viewer's, and is null without an error when the caller has no selected Profile.
    """
    media: ActiveStreamMedia
    "Seconds into the media title, as the client last reported. Null while the format attempt prepares."
    positionSeconds: Int
    "Whether the client last reported playing or paused. Null while the format attempt prepares."
    state: PlaybackState
    """
    How the current format attempt delivers the media title, including its output bitrates and its reasons.
    Null while the format attempt prepares.
    """
    decision: PlaybackDecision
    """
    The stretch of the media title that the current format attempt has produced as media segments, around the
    stream's current position. Null for direct play, while the format attempt prepares, and before any segment
    around the position exists.

    The range runs from the start of the first to the end of the last media segment of the unbroken run of
    produced segments that holds positionSeconds. After a seek it shows the run at the new position, not the
    furthest segment ever produced. When the stream has several variants, the range describes the variant whose
    media segment the player requested last. Before the player requests one, it describes the variant that the
    multivariant playlist lists first.
    """
    producedRange: MediaTimeRange
    "The worker connection that runs each running job of the stream, by its worker session id."
    workers: [String!]!
}

union ActiveStreamMedia = Movie | Episode

type ActiveStreamProfile {
    id: ID!
    "Null when the Profile was deleted while it played."
    name: String
}
